  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mo>–</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> Group and <math><mo>–</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>–</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> group have not linear geometries so they cannot cancel each other and net dipole moment is positive. Hence III and IV polar, in I and II <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi></math> cancel each other so <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub></math> is zero and they are non-polar.<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/2561a559-f650-4c18-8916-4a3f2c908cfd.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:4.69167in;height:2.00833in\" />",
